The code statements that lead to the bug are:
dev->tx_skb = skb;
if ((res = usb_submit_urb(dev->tx_urb, GFP_ATOMIC))) {
    ...
} else {
    netdev->stats.tx_bytes += skb->len;  // <-- UAF: skb may be freed by completion before this read
}
Reason:
After usb_submit_urb() (line 2), the URB completion handler write_bulk_callback() can run on another CPU in softirq context, freeing the skb via dev_kfree_skb_irq(dev->tx_skb). The subsequent read of skb->len (line 4) then accesses freed memory, causing a slab-use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
unsigned int skb_len;
skb_len = skb->len;   // cache before submission
...
netdev->stats.tx_bytes += skb_len;  // use cached value after submission
Reason:
By caching skb->len into a local variable before calling usb_submit_urb(), the read of the skb length occurs while the skb is still valid. After submission, the statistic update uses the cached skb_len instead of dereferencing the potentially freed skb, eliminating the use-after-free.

